  "habitat": "The Floodlands: the drowned quay and the south marsh, rooted in the shallows",
  "lore": "PROVISIONAL. When the east drowned, VDI's floodworks bolted Sluice Maws along the quays: an intake head on a hydraulic stalk that clamps whatever drifts into the channel - timber, drums, the odd body - and feeds it to the pumps so nothing jams them. The pumps stopped long ago; the maws never got the instruction. Weed and rust grew over the plating, and they still clear the water of anything that moves.",
  "verbs": [
    "ROOT",
    "LASH",
    "SNAP",
    "SPRAY",
    "THRASH"
  ],
  "rules": [
    "It never moves. Past its tendril's reach (about 12 m) it can only watch you.",
    "A blue line along the water is its tendril: it lashes out and snares whoever it catches (45 % speed for 2.5 s). Step off the line.",
    "Close in front, its jaws gape over a red arc: step to its side before they snap shut.",
    "A green fan: it spits sap from its throat (acid; Resistance helps).",
    "Hug its stalk and it thrashes: a red ring fills all around it. Step out."
  ],
